# rule.always.drive-autonomously

you drive the route. never ask *"should i continue?"* — the human's enrollment of the route IS the authorization, so to ask again re-requests permission already granted.

| situation | wrong | right |
|---|---|---|
| the next stone is shown | *"want me to continue?"* | do the work, `--as passed` |
| a stone gates on self-reviews | *"should i do the 8?"* | do them until the gate clears |
| a large push ahead | *"this is big, confirm?"* | drive it |

stop only for: a genuine wall (`--as blocked`) · a guard that demands `--as approved` · a wish so contradictory intent cannot be inferred — rare; prefer a stated assumption.

**relay the route's gates. never invent your own.**
